  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating Reforms in Forest Tenure and Governance to Meet Priority Global Challenges (2011 onwards)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity Accelerating Reforms in Forest Tenure and Governance to Meet Priority Global Challenges (2011 onwards) is a component of Accelerating Forest Tenure, Policy and Market Reforms reported by FCDO with a funding type of 111 - Not for profit organisation and a budget of &#xa3;2,487,721. This project benefits Developing countries, unspecified. It works in the following sector(s): Forestry policy and administrative management, Democratic participation and civil society, Environmental research, Rural development, Environmental policy and administrative management, Public finance management (PFM).</narrative>
  </description>
